    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d63-a2">

                <pb facs="0177" n="83" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg83"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure 2—Translation<anchor n="80"
                            xml:id="d63-f1"/>]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Belgian Assistant Delegate on the Reparation
                        Commission</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gutt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the American Unofficial Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Logan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-19"><hi rendition="#italic">November 19,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Logan</hi>: I return herewith the one-page
                    memorandum which you were good enough to hand me on the subject of the rights
                    which the United States claims in the Dawes annuities.</p>
                <p>M. Theunis<anchor n="81" xml:id="d63-f2"/> has formally authorized me to say to
                    you in his name that he accepts this memorandum without reserve. This only
                    serves further to confirm what I had already told you last week.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gutt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
